From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:19:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(open-items): drop the retired chat notes table

An earlier build of open items read the agent's chat for labels after
each turn and kept, per session, how far it had read and a note to give
the agent (side revision open_items0002, table open_items_chat_notes).
Items are now created only by the agent's tools, so that table has no
reader. A database that ran open_items0002 must still find that revision,
or the side store would refuse to start, so the revision is kept as it
was and open_items0003 drops the table; its downgrade recreates it. A new
database creates and drops it on the way to head.

Not proposed upstream yet.

Docs: none (storage only; nothing a caller sees changes)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
